@startuml

title Shop database - Sales orders

!include ./_common.puml

enum PaymentStatusEnum {
    unpaid
    partially_paid
    paid
    overpaid
    refunded
}

enum OrderHistorySource {
    manual
    system
    integration
}

enum OrderStatus {
    draft
    confirmed
    awaiting_stock
    ready_to_ship
    partially_shipped
    shipped
    delivered
    completed
    canceled
    partially_returned
    returned
}

enum OrderDiscountModeEnum {
    none
    rule
    manual_override
}

entity Order {
    * id: int
    * version: int
    --
    * number: string(255)
    * status: OrderStatus
    * currency: Currency
    * exchangeRateToBase: decimal(18, 8)
    customerNameSnapshot: string(255)?
    customerPhoneSnapshot: string(255)?
    customerEmailSnapshot: string(255)?
    deliveryAddress: text?
    * totalAmount: decimal(14, 4)
    * totalAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)
    discountAmount: decimal(14, 4)?
    discountAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)?
    * paidAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)
    * paymentStatus: PaymentStatusEnum
    paidAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    canceledAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    * createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
    * updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
    * store: Store
    createdBy: User?
    updatedBy: User?
    canceledBy: User?
    customer: Customer?
}

entity OrderEntry {
    * id: int
    --
    * quantity: decimal(14, 4)
    shippedQuantity: decimal(14, 4)?
    returnedQuantity: decimal(14, 4)?
    canceledQuantity: decimal(14, 4)?
    * unitPrice: decimal(14, 4)
    * unitPriceBase: decimal(14, 4)
    discountAmount: decimal(14, 4)?
    discountAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)?
    discountPercent: decimal(7, 4)?
    discountMode: OrderDiscountModeEnum?
    discountRuleNameSnapshot: string(255)?
    * totalPrice: decimal(14, 4)
    * totalPriceBase: decimal(14, 4)
    * productNameSnapshot: string(255)
    * productCodeSnapshot: string(255)
    * unitCodeSnapshot: string(50)
    * unitNameSnapshot: string(255)
    * order: Order
    * product: Product
    warehouse: Warehouse?
    warehouseStockBatch: WarehouseStockBatch?
    discountRule: ProductDiscountRule?
}

entity OrderComment {
    * id: int
    --
    * body: text
    * createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
    updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    deletedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    * order: Order
    * author: User
}

entity OrderHistory {
    * id: int
    --
    * eventKey: string(100)
    * source: OrderHistorySource
    * title: string(255)
    description: text?
    changes: json?
    payload: json?
    relatedEntityType: string(100)?
    relatedEntityId: int?
    * occurredAt: DateTimeImmutable
    actorNameSnapshot: string(255)?
    * order: Order
    actor: User?
}


Store ||--o{ Order : receives
Currency ||--o{ Order : order currency
Customer |o--o{ Order : places
OrderStatus ||--o{ Order : controls
PaymentStatusEnum ||--o{ Order : payment state
Order ||--o{ OrderEntry : has
Order |o--o{ Payment : paid by
Order ||--o{ InventoryDocument : generates stock docs
Product ||--o{ OrderEntry : ordered as
Warehouse |o--o{ OrderEntry : ships from
WarehouseStockBatch |o--o{ OrderEntry : priced/reserved from
ProductDiscountRule |o--o{ OrderEntry : discount source
Order ||--o{ OrderComment : has comments
Order ||--o{ OrderHistory : has timeline
Order |o--o{ PaymentHistory : shows payment events
User ||--o{ OrderComment : authors
User |o--o{ OrderHistory : performs
OrderHistorySource ||--o{ OrderHistory : classifies source
OrderEntry |o--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : ships/returns
OrderEntry ||--o{ StockReservation : reserves

note right of Order
  Customer is optional to allow quick one-time orders.
  createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy are audit fields for admin accountability.
  canceledAt should be filled when status becomes canceled.
  customerNameSnapshot/customerPhoneSnapshot/customerEmailSnapshot store contact data at order time.
  Free-form communication is stored in OrderComment rows, not on Order itself.
  Operational order timeline is stored in OrderHistory rows.
  The visible admin history also merges linked PaymentHistory events.

  currency stores the original sale currency.
  exchangeRateToBase is a snapshot: 1 order currency = X Store.baseCurrency.
  totalAmount is in original currency; totalAmountBase is in Store.baseCurrency.
end note

note right of OrderComment
  Human discussion attached to an order.
  One order can have many comments from different users.

  Comments are separate from operational history:
  - OrderComment stores the message body.
  - OrderHistory records that a comment was added/edited/deleted.

  deletedAt is optional soft delete so the UI can hide a comment
  without destroying the audit trail.
end note

note right of OrderHistory
  Dedicated append-only timeline for Order.
  This is richer than StatusHistory and is the source of truth
  for the future human-readable order activity feed.

  eventKey is a stable machine key, for example:
  order.created, order.status_changed, order.comment_added,
  order.entry_updated, order.delivery_declaration_generated.

  source separates manual, system and integration events.
  actor can be null for automatic events; actorNameSnapshot preserves
  the display name that should be shown later in the timeline.

  title/description store ready-to-display human-readable snapshots.
  changes stores structured before/after values for changed fields.
  payload stores extra structured data for future features:
  delivery service, declaration number, shipping payer,
  integration response, automation context and similar details.

  relatedEntityType/relatedEntityId can link future order-side records
  without changing the base timeline model each time.
end note

note right of PaymentHistory
  PaymentHistory rows are append-only financial timeline events.
  They are displayed together with OrderHistory in the order admin history,
  but Payment remains the financial source of truth.
end note

note right of OrderStatus
  Recommended order flow:
  draft -> confirmed -> awaiting_stock -> ready_to_ship -> partially_shipped -> shipped -> delivered -> completed.

  canceled is for orders stopped before completion.
  partially_returned/returned are post-shipment states.
  Backorders usually use awaiting_stock until enough stock is produced, purchased or reserved.
end note

note right of OrderEntry
  Sales order line.
  Stores snapshot of product name, code, unit code/name, quantity and sale price at the moment of order.
  Monetary fields without Base suffix are in Order.currency. Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.
  warehouseStockBatch is optional and identifies the FIFO batch used for stock-backed pricing/reservation.
  Search should expose different batches as separate stock options, ordered oldest first.
  Each stock-backed OrderEntry should keep one selected batch and one sale price snapshot.
  discountRule/discountPercent/discountMode record the configured or manual discount source.
  discountAmount remains the money snapshot used by totals.
  Manual override and below-cost discounted lines require order.discount.override.

  shippedQuantity, returnedQuantity and canceledQuantity are denormalized progress/cache fields
  for fast UI and filtering. Source of truth is InventoryDocumentLine + posted StockMovement.
  If cache becomes inconsistent, recalculate it from posted inventory documents.

  Partial shipments are allowed:
  one OrderEntry can be linked to multiple InventoryDocumentLine rows over time.
  Backordered quantity = quantity - shippedQuantity - canceledQuantity, with reservations handled separately.

  InventoryDocumentLine is created from this line when stock is shipped or returned.
end note

@enduml
